"Task:
Generate a complete HTML file for a one-page website for a prompt engineering platform called PromptForge. This platform provides resources, templates, and tools to help users craft effective prompts. Your output must include the HTML structure, embedded CSS (inside a <style> tag within the <head> section), and JavaScript (inside a <script> tag at the end of the <body> section). Be sure to include inline comments throughout the code to explain each part.

Requirements:

1. Navigation Bar:

Create a fixed navigation bar at the top of the page.

Include links to key sections: Home, Templates, Tools, and Community.

Add a search bar within the navigation bar for users to quickly find prompt templates.



2. Hero Section:

Design a hero section featuring a video background (use a placeholder for the video URL).

Display a dynamic tagline that rotates through the following phrases every 3 seconds:

“Unlock Your Creativity”

“Craft Perfect Prompts”

“Transform Ideas into Reality”


Include a “Get Started” button that links to the Templates section.



3. Featured Templates Section:

Display several template cards in a grid layout.

Each template card should include placeholders for:

A template preview image

Template title

A brief description of the use case

(Optional) User rating




4. Tools & Resources Section:

Create an interactive section titled “Tools & Resources.”

Integrate a short interactive element (such as a form or a series of buttons) that helps users select appropriate prompt engineering tools based on their needs.

Provide a button to explore the available tools.



5. Success Stories Section:

Develop a testimonials section with placeholders for testimonial text and user names.

This section should highlight positive feedback from users who have enhanced their prompt engineering workflow.



6. Footer:

Include links to the platform’s Blog, FAQ, and Privacy Policy.

Add a “Contact Us” button that opens a modal window.

The modal should contain a contact form and support information.



7. Additional Instructions:

Use filler placeholder content for the video background, template cards, and testimonials.

Ensure all styles are embedded within the <style> tag in the <head>.

Place all JavaScript code within the <script> tag at the end of the <body>.

The JavaScript must implement the dynamic tagline rotation in the hero section, switching the displayed tagline every 3 seconds.




Output Format:
Return a complete, self-contained HTML document that meets the above specifications. The code should be well-organized and commented for clarity."
